  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal agencies obligated a total of $18.4B in Pennsylvania. Those obligations came in 358,356 awards with an average award size of $51.2K. Obligations fell 31.9% year over year, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The Department of Defense accounted for the largest share with $14.6B in obligations. Other major buyers include the Department of Energy with $2B and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $589M. At the vendor level, AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP received $4.5B and FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC received $4B. Industry concentration is visible in a few NAICS sectors: Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $4.5B, and Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing received $3B. Past fiscal years show higher totals, including $26.9B in FY25 and $26.6B in FY24, underscoring that FY2026 to date is a partial-year picture relative to prior full fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal contracting in Pennsylvania?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $14.6B in obligations. The Department of Energy follows with $2B, then the Department of Veterans Affairs with $589M and Health and Human Services with $272M. Several civilian agencies also appear on the list, including Commerce at $222M and Agriculture at $185M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Pennsylvania?",
        "body": "AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP is the top vendor with $4.5B in obligations, followed by FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC at $4B and BECHTEL PLANT MACHINERY, INC. at $2.1B. THE BOEING COMPANY received $1.8B, and a mix of defense, health, and academic contractors fill the rest of the top ten list."
      }
    ]
  },
